---
title: Connecting a hotel system (DEC-017, DEC-021)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor O as Hotel owner
    participant W as Website (host mode)
    participant A as Django API
    participant X as Hotel system (channel manager or PMS)
    participant J as Sync job and outbox worker
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    actor M as Admin
    O->>W: Chooses "Connect my hotel system", enters system and access key
    W->>A: POST /host/integrations
    A->>A: URL check (https, public address only)
    A->>X: test call with the key
    X-->>A: ok, property found
    A->>DB: save connection (key encrypted), status active
    A-)J: first import
    J->>X: read room types, prices, availability, services
    X-->>J: data
    J->>DB: create or update room types, nights, services (marked as imported)
    J->>DB: write sync log (what changed)
    A-->>W: connection active, rooms and services listed
    loop every 15 minutes (reconciliation pass)
        J->>X: read changes
        J->>DB: update availability and prices, never total below held + booked
        opt hotel asks for fewer rooms than BLADUS sold
            J->>DB: clamp total to held + booked, open an inventory conflict
            M->>A: GET /admin/inventory-conflicts
            M->>A: POST /admin/inventory-conflicts/{conflict_id}/resolve
        end
    end
    Note over A,J: every BLADUS booking change writes an inventory.push outbox message, sent at once
    J->>X: push the new availability (retries, then dead)
    M->>A: GET /admin/outbox?status=dead
    M->>A: POST /admin/outbox/{message_id}/retry
